# The Syringe Gun's needles (real TF2; ours: the needle part of
# launch.scene, run with fov_desired 75). This account's Medic doesn't
# carry the stock gun, so a puppet Medic bot (stock loadout; its slot chosen
# again once spawned, or it keeps its Medi Gun) fires (`bot_forceattack`)
# and we watch: in its eyes (`spec_mode 4`: FOV 75) down 2fort's bridge
# (`fly_NN`, every frame at 60 a second for 0.67
# s: where a needle first shows, its trail). What needles do on a wall
# was seen by hand (a Medic bot facing 2fort's wall at 0 500, needles
# into it, then a free spectator beside the marks): see
# specs/tf2/effects.md, "Measured".
#   tools/tf2ref/tf2ref.py scene tools/tf2ref/scenes/needles.tf2 --out <dir>
mp_disable_respawn_times 1
cl_drawhud 0
r_drawvgui 0
r_drawviewmodel 1
tf_spec_xray 0
fov_desired 90
viewmodel_fov 54
fps_max 60
mat_colorcorrection 0
tf_weapon_criticals 0
host_framerate 0
bot_kick all
sleep 1
jointeam spectator
sleep 2
bot_selectweaponslot 0
bot -name RefMedic -class medic -team red
sleep 3
bot_teleport RefMedic 0 -300 0 0 90 0
bot_selectweaponslot 0
sleep 2
spec_player RefMedic
sleep 1
spec_mode 4
sleep 1
bot_teleport RefMedic 0 -300 0 0 90 0
sleep 3
shot fly_idle
host_framerate 0.016667
movie fly
wait 2
bot_forceattack 1
wait 40
bot_forceattack 0
wait 40
endmovie
host_framerate 0
sleep 1
bot_kick all
